# Neo Audio to MIDI parameters (docs/specs/audio-to-midi.md). The order changes only with a version (machines.md §3.2): songs and presets
# store values by position. Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoAudioToMidi
namespace NeoBuzz.AudioToMidi
class NeoAudioToMidiMachine
summary Turns a live mono instrument into MIDI and lets the audio pass through (monitor blend 0 to 100 %). Melody mode (guitar, bass, keys, wind, synth lines): a note at each onset with its velocity from the attack, or at the first clean pitch; plucks, re-plucks, hammer-ons and slides handled; a minimum note length, legato, an optional key or scale lock, octave shift, and pitch bend (plus or minus 1 to 12 semitones) so slides and vibrato come through; Fast (the note plays as soon as its pitch is clear, and is corrected within 80 ms) or Stable (waits for a settled pitch). Drums mode (a drum kit, a pad, a percussive instrument): kick, snare and hat notes with no training, each with its own note, velocity, sensitivity and minimum interval, and an optional calibration of five hits each. The MIDI goes to a target machine, to an external MIDI device, and is a MIDI From source for armed tracks. Use it to play a synth from a guitar or bass, to turn a drum kit into a drum machine's triggers, or to record a performance as a clip.

group Input
Monitor "Monitor" 0 100 100 pct 0 | Dry audio at the output: 0 is silent, 100 % is the input as it came
    how Sets how much of the dry instrument reaches the output, from 0% (silent) to 100% (as it came in).
    sound At 0% you hear only what the synth plays from the MIDI; a little dry signal gives the player a feel of the strings.
Mode "Mode" 0 1 0 enum Melody Drums | Melody: one note at a time, with its pitch. Drums: kick, snare and hat hits
    how Chooses what the input is turned into: a melody (notes with a pitch) or drum hits (kick, snare, hat).
    sound Melody follows the pitch of a guitar, bass or keys; Drums ignores pitch and names each hit by its sound.
Range "Range" 0 2 0 enum Guitar Bass Full | The lowest and highest note it listens for: Guitar (80 Hz to 1.2 kHz, about 16 ms), Bass (38 to 400 Hz, about 33 ms), Full (38 Hz to 2 kHz, about 33 ms)
    how Chooses the pitch range: Guitar (from 80 Hz, about 16 ms), Bass (from 38 Hz, about 33 ms) or Full (38 Hz to 2 kHz, about 33 ms).
    sound A narrower range answers sooner; Bass and Full see the lowest notes of a bass but each note starts a little later.
Level "Level" 0 50 30 lin -70 -20 dB 0 | The quietest signal that plays a note: under this level nothing starts
    how Sets the quietest level, from -70 to -20 dB, that starts a note or a hit.
    sound Raising it ignores amp hum, string noise and bleed; set too high it misses soft playing.
Sensitivity "Sensitivity" 0 100 50 pct 0 | How soft an attack may be and still start a note or a hit (the onset threshold)
    how Sets how soft an attack may be and still count, from 0 to 100%.
    sound Higher values catch soft plucks and ghost notes and risk noise, fret buzz and bleed.
Response "Response" 0 1 0 enum Fast Stable | Fast plays a note as soon as its pitch is clear and corrects it within 80 ms; Stable waits Settle ms first
    how Chooses when a new note starts: Fast plays it at the first clean pitch and corrects it within 80 ms if it was another note (or by pitch bend when that is on); Stable waits Settle ms of the same note before playing it.
    sound Fast feels immediate for live playing and may retrigger once on a muddy attack; Stable never plays a wrong first note but answers later.
group Melody
Retrigger "Retrigger" 0 1 1 switch | A new attack of the note already sounding plays it again (a re-pluck); off ignores attacks while a note sounds
    how Switches playing a note again on each new attack, even of the same pitch, on or off.
    sound On, every pluck of the same string plays a new note; off suits sustained instruments whose attack is not a new note.
Lock "Lock" 0 3 0 enum Off Set_key Song_key Suggest | Off: every semitone. Set key: the Root and Scale. Song key: the key of the song (the song's Key entry), else Root and Scale. Suggest: the key found from the notes played so far
    how Chooses how notes are kept to a key: Off, the Root and Scale, the song's key or a key found from what you played.
    sound Locked notes land on the key whatever the instrument does; Off follows every semitone, which is what most instruments want.
Root "Root" 0 11 0 enum C "C#" D "D#" E F "F#" G "G#" A "A#" B | The key's root note
    how Sets the key's root note from C to B.
    sound It moves every in-key note with it; the scale keyboard shows the result.
Scale "Scale" 0 13 0 enum Major Minor Dorian Phrygian Lydian Mixolydian Locrian Harmonic_minor Melodic_minor Major_pentatonic Minor_pentatonic Blues Whole_tone Custom | The scale the notes are locked to
    how Chooses the scale of the key from 14 choices, including a Custom set of notes.
    sound Major sounds bright, minor darker, pentatonic and blues leave out the notes that clash.
Custom "Custom notes" 0 4095 2741 int 0 | The notes of the Custom scale, one bit per note from C (bit 0) to B
    how Holds the Custom scale's twelve notes, one bit each from C to B.
    sound Only the notes you switch on in the keyboard can play when Scale is Custom.
Octave "Octave" 0 6 3 int -3 oct signed | Octave shift of the notes
    how Shifts the notes by whole octaves, from -3 to +3.
    sound A bass can play a synth bass an octave higher, or a guitar a synth lead two octaves up.
Stick "Stickiness" 0 100 25 lin 0 100 cents 0 | How far past the middle between two notes the pitch must go before the note changes (a hysteresis)
    how Sets how far past the middle between two notes the pitch must go before the note changes, from 0 to 100 cents.
    sound More stickiness holds a bent or wobbly note steady; none follows every small move.
Settle "Settle" 0 200 25 lin 0 200 ms 0 | How long a new pitch must be held before it replaces the note sounding (and, in Stable response, before a note first plays)
    how Sets how long a new pitch must be held before it replaces the note sounding, from 0 to 200 ms; in Stable response it also delays the first note.
    sound Longer settling removes grace notes and brief slides at the cost of a later note start.
MinNote "Min note length" 0 100 6 lin 0 500 ms 0 | A note lasts at least this long, however short the sound was
    how Sets the shortest a note lasts, from 0 to 100 mapped to 0 to 500 ms.
    sound Short plucked notes still last long enough for the synth to sound.
Release "Release" 0 34 14 lin 6 40 dB 0 | The note ends when the level falls this far under its peak (or the pitch is lost)
    how Sets how far the level must fall under the note's peak, from 6 to 40 dB, before the note ends.
    sound A small drop ends notes with the pluck; a large one lets them ring out with the string's decay.
Legato "Legato" 0 1 0 switch | A new note starts before the old one stops (for mono synths with legato), instead of after
    how Starts a new note before the old one stops when switched on.
    sound Mono synths then glide between notes instead of retriggering.
Bend "Pitch bend" 0 12 0 enum Off "±1 st" "±2 st" "±3 st" "±4 st" "±5 st" "±6 st" "±7 st" "±8 st" "±9 st" "±10 st" "±11 st" "±12 st" | Pitch bend range: the pitch's distance from the note is sent as bend, so slides and vibrato come through. Set the same range on the synth
    how Sets the pitch bend range from off to plus or minus 12 semitones.
    sound Slides, bends and vibrato of the instrument move the synth's pitch by the same amount; set the synth to the same range.
BendMode "Bend mode" 0 1 0 enum Free Anchored | Free: bend follows every wobble. Anchored: the note stays put until the pitch moves farther than the Anchor from its middle, then it bends
    how Chooses Free bend or Anchored bend.
    sound Free follows every wobble; Anchored keeps the note still until the pitch leaves it, then bends.
Anchor "Anchor" 5 100 35 lin 5 100 cents 0 | Anchored bend: how far from the note's middle the pitch must move before the bend starts
    how Sets how far from the note's middle the pitch must move, from 5 to 100 cents, before the bend starts.
    sound A larger anchor keeps vibrato from bending the note; a small one bends at once.
VelMode "Velocity" 0 1 0 enum Dynamic Fixed | Dynamic: from how hard the note was attacked. Fixed: always the Fixed velocity
    how Chooses note velocity from the attack (Dynamic) or always the Fixed velocity.
    sound Dynamic plays soft picking softly; Fixed gives every note the same strength.
Fixed "Fixed velocity" 1 127 100 int 0 | The velocity of every note in Fixed mode, and the loudest in Dynamic
    how Sets the fixed velocity, and the loudest in Dynamic, from 1 to 127.
    sound Higher values play louder or brighter on most synths.
VelMin "Softest velocity" 1 127 25 int 0 | Dynamic: the velocity of the softest note
    how Sets the velocity of the softest note in Dynamic mode, from 1 to 127.
    sound A higher minimum keeps soft notes audible.
Soft "Soft level" 0 50 20 lin -70 -20 dB 0 | Dynamic: the attack level that gives the softest velocity
    how Sets the attack level, from -70 to -20 dB, that gives the softest velocity.
    sound Raise it if soft playing sounds too loud on the synth.
Loud "Loud level" 0 40 28 lin -40 0 dB 0 | Dynamic: the attack level that gives the loudest velocity
    how Sets the attack level, from -40 to 0 dB, that gives the loudest velocity.
    sound Lower it so ordinary playing reaches full velocity.
NoteCh "Note channel" 0 15 0 int 1 | MIDI channel of the notes
    how Sets the MIDI channel of the notes, from 1 to 16.
    sound It selects which synth or part plays the line.
group Drums
Length "Hit length" 0 490 50 lin 10 500 ms 0 | How long each drum note is held before its note off
    how Sets how long each drum note is held, from 10 to 500 ms.
    sound Short notes suit drums that ring by themselves; long ones suit sustained sounds.
DrumCh "Drum channel" 0 15 9 int 1 | MIDI channel of the drum notes (10 is the drum channel)
    how Sets the MIDI channel of the drum notes, from 1 to 16.
    sound Channel 10 is the drum channel of most drum machines.
KickNote "Kick note" 0 127 36 int 0 | MIDI note of the kick
    how Sets the MIDI note the kick plays, from 0 to 127.
    sound Choose the drum you want the kick to play; the default follows the usual drum map.
KickVel "Kick velocity" 0 127 0 int 0 | 0: from how hard the hit was. 1 to 127: always this velocity
    how Sets the kick's velocity from 1 to 127, or 0 to take it from how hard the hit was.
    sound Zero makes harder hits play louder; a number makes every hit the same.
KickSens "Kick sensitivity" 0 100 50 pct 0 | How readily a hit counts as a kick: higher plays more of the doubtful hits
    how Sets how readily a hit counts as a kick, from 0 to 100%.
    sound Higher values play more kicks but let other drums through as one; lower ones play only clear kicks.
KickGap "Kick interval" 0 290 50 lin 10 300 ms 0 | The shortest time between two kicks
    how Sets the shortest time between two kicks, from 10 to 300 ms.
    sound A kick's tail can look like a second hit; a longer interval ignores it, a short one lets double kicks through.
SnareNote "Snare note" 0 127 38 int 0 | MIDI note of the snare
    how Sets the MIDI note the snare plays, from 0 to 127.
    sound Choose the drum you want the snare to play; the default follows the usual drum map.
SnareVel "Snare velocity" 0 127 0 int 0 | 0: from how hard the hit was. 1 to 127: always this velocity
    how Sets the snare's velocity from 1 to 127, or 0 to take it from how hard the hit was.
    sound Zero makes harder hits play louder, ghost notes included; a number makes every hit the same.
SnareSens "Snare sensitivity" 0 100 50 pct 0 | How readily a hit counts as a snare: higher plays more of the doubtful hits
    how Sets how readily a hit counts as a snare, from 0 to 100%.
    sound Higher values play more snares and ghost notes but let other drums through as one.
SnareGap "Snare interval" 0 290 30 lin 10 300 ms 0 | The shortest time between two snare hits
    how Sets the shortest time between two snare hits, from 10 to 300 ms.
    sound Long enough to ignore a rim's ring, short enough for rolls and ghost notes.
HatNote "Hat note" 0 127 42 int 0 | MIDI note of the hat
    how Sets the MIDI note the hat plays, from 0 to 127.
    sound Choose the drum you want the hat to play; the default is the closed hat.
HatVel "Hat velocity" 0 127 0 int 0 | 0: from how hard the hit was. 1 to 127: always this velocity
    how Sets the hat's velocity from 1 to 127, or 0 to take it from how hard the hit was.
    sound Zero makes harder hits play louder; a number makes every hit the same.
HatSens "Hat sensitivity" 0 100 50 pct 0 | How readily a hit counts as a hat: higher plays more of the doubtful hits
    how Sets how readily a hit counts as a hat, from 0 to 100%.
    sound Higher values play more hat hits but let the snare's wires and cymbals through as one.
HatGap "Hat interval" 0 290 15 lin 10 300 ms 0 | The shortest time between two hat hits
    how Sets the shortest time between two hat hits, from 10 to 300 ms.
    sound Hats run fast: a short interval lets sixteenths and thirty-seconds through.
